==Strategy==
All enemies have very short range, which means that most [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red cats]], [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel cats]] and [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark cats]] will do well in this stage. Some good examples are [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hip Hop Cat]], [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]], [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch Cat]], [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sexy Bathtub Cat]], [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]], [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet Cat]] and [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]]. If you are later in the game however, most of these stages can be easily rushed.

==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 11.5 Update|version 11.5]], this stage had a restriction of "only [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal]], [[:Category:Special Cats|Special]], [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]] and [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare]] units", rather than a Cat Deploy Limit of 10.

